  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to local communities in their efforts to ensure their rights within Nacala diocese</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to ensure the rights of communities in the Diocese of Nacala, Mozambique. The project is inserted into the pastoral activity plan of the Diocesan Justice and Peace Commission.

There are four main areas of work: 

1) Training youth and community awareness to ensure the protection of rights in communities, specifically those that have to do with land use. 
2) Legal advice to ensure the protection of the rights of communities primarily in respect of land use.
3) Monitoring of Public Policy, starting with developing community awareness and training.  
4) Establish networks with other NGOs at national or international level to increase the level of effectiveness of our actions for the benefit of communities.</narrative>
  </description>
